# Pinned zero-model canary outcomes for eval/harness_acceptance.sh (engine pin: FORGE_COMMIT).
# Re-pin DELIBERATELY, with the commit that moved a number, never to make a run pass.
# floor/floor never builds a play menu; random/random reaches the full menu (see CLAUDE.md).
floor.seed=42
floor.winner=A
floor.turns=108
# 2026-10-12: G7 routed chooseStartingPlayer/chooseColor/chooseSomeType/chooseProtectionType then
# chooseCardsToDiscardToMaximumHandSize/chooseCardsToDelve from Forge AI to the model. The floor arm
# now takes the deterministic fronts (was AI); decisions moved 1004 -> 1005 -> 1053 (same winner/turns).
# 2026-10-13: engine pin bumped c1c64a53 -> 6c1810dd0b42 (3 months upstream). The floor arm is
# deterministic, but the ENGINE changed (card scripts, AI, rules handling). Same winner AND turns;
# decisions 1053 -> 1064. Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped.
# 2026-10-13 (later): the seat may respond to its OWN trigger on the stack (it used to auto-pass
# without a row). The floor arm reaches that window 4 times and takes its usual
# play(no-budget)->PASS, so 4 more auto rows are written: 1064 -> 1068. Same winner, same turns,
# no game action changed. Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0.
# 2026-10-16: epochs 33/34 (#216 "say a spell on the stack is not yet resolved", #218 "counterspells
# counter, announced values are asked") widened the play-menu windows the seat is offered, and both
# landed while the canary stage could not run at all (the #219 parse break: every stage list died
# after classpath on this machine's bash 3.2). The floor arm's game line is IDENTICAL (winner A,
# 108 turns); its deterministic policy now answers far more play windows: 1068 -> 1804 decision
# rows (1722 of them play rows), all tier=auto, 0 Forge-AI rows (the substring hits "Faithless"
# /"stained" are text matches only), 0 silent drops, game not capped. Same counts on two runs
# (OUT=runs/harness-acceptance/pr220-183730 and runs/harness-acceptance/repin-confirm2-185550).
# Re-pinned deliberately.
# Attribution bound: the gate did not parse from 21c6b9ba (merge of #182, 2026-10-15) until
# 74013565, so no canary measured anything in between; epochs 33/34 are the named movers the
# twice-validated head-tree counts are consistent with, not the proven exclusives of the shift.
# linux.floor.* below are STALE for #216/#218 still; no Linux environment is available here.
floor.decisions=1804
random.seed=42
# 2026-09-07: model-owned optional confirmations expose four previously silent AI
# trigger choices to the random policy (first divergence: confirm-trigger, turn 15, decision 61).
# 2026-10-12: G7 routing (above) now exposes play/draw, colour, type, protection, cleanup-discard and
# delve choices to the random policy too; the game diverges far earlier. Reproduced.
# 2026-10-12 (later): simultaneous-trigger ORDER is model-owned too; the random policy now permutes
# trigger order, moving the game again (17 turns / 75 decisions, winner B). Reproduced.
# 2026-10-13: engine pin bumped c1c64a53 -> 6c1810dd0b42. The random arm is a random walk over the
# legal menu, so ANY engine change re-rolls the whole game: now winner A, 29 turns / 167 decisions.
# Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped. Random is a floor ANCHOR, not a
# behavioural contract -- its job is to move deterministically under a fixed engine, which it does.
# 2026-10-13 (later): sacrifice-as-cost moved from Forge AI to the seat on the real play path
# (playChosenSpellAbility override; see OWNERSHIP.md "Correction"). The random arm now makes those
# choices itself -- 13 sacrifice decisions appear in the game log that were previously silent -- so
# the random walk re-rolls: winner A, 26 turns / 171 decisions. Floor is unchanged (it never plays).
# Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped.
# 2026-10-13 (later): one creature that can attack, and one scried or surveiled card, are decisions
# again instead of "forced-only-legal" shortcuts (attack with it / keep it, unasked). The random arm
# now rolls those too, so its walk re-rolls: winner B, 19 turns / 65 decisions. Reproduced twice
# (/tmp/acc-fbef9cfab, /tmp/acc-part). Floor is unchanged: it attacks with everything and never scries.
# 2026-10-14: engine pin bumped 6c1810dd0b42 -> 34a8662b7966 (10 upstream commits, tip "fix
# vprompt"). The floor arm did NOT move (A/108/1068 above, unchanged). The random arm re-rolled
# as it does on any engine change and now reproduces at B/33/307 (twice, same class-load build).
# Re-pinned deliberately: ai=0 rows, silent drops=0, game not capped. This also refreshes the Mac
# random pin that #112 recorded as stale (B/19/65 was unreproducible on this machine).
# The linux.* pins below are ANOTHER ENVIRONMENT's (a Linux container, #95/#112). They do not affect
# this Mac dev checkout, where the plain keys above are used; Mac development does not maintain them.
# 2026-10-15: the "already passed here" check no longer applies to the random arm (it is a uniform
# baseline over every window, and the check is a model-call saving) and now keys on the stack. The
# random arm used to skip 12 windows with something castable (t:"window" rows, reason last-sig);
# it now rolls them, so its walk re-rolls: winner B, 32 turns / 173 decisions. Reproduced twice
# (/tmp/acc-sig2, /tmp/acc-sig3). Floor unchanged (it never builds a menu). The linux.* random pins
# below are STALE for this change; no Linux run was available.
# 2026-10-15 (later): trigger targets are the seat's (orderAndPlaySimultaneousSa, playTrigger), so the
# random arm now picks them instead of Forge AI's doTrigger and its walk re-rolls: winner B, 26 turns /
# 144 decisions. Reproduced twice (/tmp/acc-tr2, /tmp/acc-tr3). Floor unchanged. linux.* random STALE.
# 2026-10-15 (later): a spell cast by an effect is the seat's (playSaFromPlayEffect: cast-or-not, X,
# modes, targets), as are discard costs, "unless" payments and votes. The random walk's first new
# decisions are two play-from-effect rows (first divergence), and it re-rolls: winner B, 30 turns / 164
# decisions. Reproduced twice (/tmp/acc-lk2, /tmp/acc-lk3). Floor unchanged. linux.* random STALE.
# 2026-10-15 (later): which mana sources stay untapped is the seat's (holdManaSources); the random arm
# now holds a random subset 26 times in the game ("mana: keep untapped" lines), so its walk re-rolls:
# winner B, 70 turns / 438 decisions. Reproduced twice (/tmp/acc-mana2, /tmp/acc-mana3). Floor
# unchanged (never asked). linux.* random STALE.
# 2026-10-16: the same two epochs re-rolled the random walk again (same #219 blind spot): stable at
# winner B, 70 turns; decisions 438 -> 450, all tier=auto, 0 Forge-AI rows, 0 silent drops, game not
# capped (two runs as the floor re-pin above). linux.* random below are STALE for #216/#218 still.
random.winner=B
random.turns=70
random.decisions=450
# Silent Forge-AI strategic/payment hooks reachable in Legacy play (ControllerOwnershipTest baseline).
# 2026-10-15: trigger targets and modes are the seat's (orderAndPlaySimultaneousSa, playTrigger
# overridden; Forge AI's doTrigger chose every trigger target before). 3 -> 1.
# 2026-10-15: the any-colour shard colour is the seat's (engine patch, docs/harness/ENGINE-PATCHES.md). 1 -> 0.
ownership.silent_ai_strategic_max=0
# 2026-10-14: LINUX pins (PR #95). The same commit plays seed 42 differently on Linux (Debian
# container, Xvfb) than on the reference Mac, so the canaries are pinned per OS; a "linux." key wins
# over the plain key there, and the plain keys stay the Mac's. Floor is A/108/1081 on Linux at every
# commit tried -- 6686ceb (the Mac pin of 1068 already in force), 37cff95, main b425298 and this PR -- so
# no commit moved it; 13 more auto rows, same winner and turns. Not the cause: JDK 17 vs 21, CPU count
# (-XX:ActiveProcessorCount=1 and 12), locale (C.UTF-8), timezone. Not yet found.
# Random differs by OS too: on Linux it is B/16/94 at a955cd8 (where the Mac pin B/19/65 was set; JDK
# 17 and 21) and at main b425298. Random on Linux is A/56/290 at this PR, reproduced 5 times (JDK 17,
# CPU 1/4/12, C.UTF-8, TZ); this PR moves the random arm on every OS (it now casts alternative-cost
# spells and picks what exile and return costs take). The Mac pin was re-measured on 2026-10-14 (B/33/307,
# above); the docs describe the OS difference. The linux.* pins below are that environment's, kept
# for a Linux runner, not a Mac-dev requirement.
linux.floor.winner=A
linux.floor.turns=108
# 2026-10-15 (feat/no-heuristics): the harness shortcuts are off by default. Floor on Linux is A/108/1824:
# the same game (winner and turns unchanged), with 743 more rows for windows the skip heuristics used
# to pass silently. Measured: with SKIP_HEURISTICS=1 MULLIGAN_HEURISTIC=1 ONE_TIER=0 the same build
# plays A/108/1081, the old pin, so the default flip is the whole change. Random is unchanged (A/45/368;
# its arm bypasses the heuristics). The Mac floor pin is STALE until measured there.
# 2026-10-15 (fix/no-engine-fallback-rare): chooseSingleReplacementEffect and chooseCounterType are the
# seat's now (they were Forge AI's, with no row). Floor reaches four replacement-effect choices with one
# legal option each, now recorded as replacement-order(forced-only-legal): A/108/1828. Every other row,
# the winner and the turns are unchanged (diffed per type against fix/no-engine-fallback's run). The Mac
# floor pin is STALE until measured there.
linux.floor.decisions=1828
# 2026-10-15: Linux random re-measured at the head of the #143-#156 stack (fix/engine-id-leak) in a
# Debian cloud container (JDK 17, engine 34a8662b), where the stack's Mac-only re-pins had left it STALE:
# A/45/368, reproduced three times with the same class-load build. Floor unchanged on Linux (A/108/1081).
# Both OS pin sets are kept so one checkout passes on the Mac laptop and on a Linux server; a change
# that moves the random walk re-pins the OS it was measured on and marks the other STALE until measured.
linux.random.winner=A
linux.random.turns=45
# 2026-10-15 (fix/no-engine-fallback-rare): six replacement-order and two counter-type choices with one
# legal option each are now recorded (forced-only-legal): A/45/376, the same game otherwise (diffed per
# type). The Mac random pin is STALE until measured there.
linux.random.decisions=376
